  "notes": "USAGE:\nAlso used as a noun: {暴露|ばくろ} (exposure, revelation). The compound {暴露|ばくろ}{本|ぼん} (exposé book) is a common collocation. Carries a stronger, more dramatic tone than {明|あ}かす or {公開|こうかい}する.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {秘密|ひみつ}を{暴露|ばくろ}する (to expose a secret)\n- {不正|ふせい}を{暴露|ばくろ}する (to expose wrongdoing)\n- {暴露|ばくろ}{本|ぼん} (exposé; tell-all book)\n- {暴露|ばくろ}{記事|きじ} (exposé article)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {明|あ}かす: to reveal, to disclose — more neutral; can be used for personal confessions\n- {告発|こくはつ}する: to accuse, to report — focuses on formally reporting wrongdoing, often to authorities",
